      "writtenOn": "2016-11-29T01:18:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Consider instead:\n\n(top-level)\n  uint8_t ConvertHidlReportEventFlagToLegacyReportEventFlag(StaBackgroundScanBucketEventReportSchemeMask hidl_flag) {\n      using HidlFlag \u003d StaBackgroundScanBucketEventReportSchemeMask;\n      switch (hidl_flag) {\n          case HidlFlag::EACH_SCAN:\n              return REPORT_EVENTS_EACH_SCAN;\n          // ...\n      };\n  }\n\n(at line 59)\n  using HidlFlag \u003d StaBackgroundScanBucketEventReportSchemeMask;\n  for (const auto flag : {HidlFlag::EACH_SCAN, ...}) {\n      if (hidl_bucket_spec.eventReportScheme \u0026 static_cast\u003cstd::underlying_type\u003cHidlFlag\u003e::type\u003e(flag)) {\n          legacy_bucket_spec.report_events |\u003d\n               ConvertHidlReportEventFlagToLegacyReportEventFlag(flag);\n      }\n  }\n\nAdvantages of this structuring:\n1) using a loop makes it obvious that there\u0027s a common behavior across values\n2) using underlying_type makes it clear that the cast is safe\n3) moving the mapping to a separate function makes it easier to review the mapping\n4) using a switch for the mapping enables the compiler to check that we\u0027ve covered all the cases (all the values in the enum)",
