      "writtenOn": "2016-11-29T01:18:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m not sure that emplace_back() makes sense here. AIUI, the point of emplace_back is to avoid creation of a temporary, by forwarding the parameters to the element\u0027s ctor.\n\nSo the idiomatic use of emplace_back would be something like\n\n  hidl_ie_elements-\u003eemplace_back(id, ie_element-\u003edata, ie_element-\u003elen);\n\nThat\u0027s assuming that WifiInformationElement had a ctor with the appropriate arguments. But WIE does not have such a ctor. \n\nSo, instead, we use emplace_back to call the copy ctor. That works, but I don\u0027t believe it\u0027s any more efficient than push_back.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 117,
        "startChar": 22,
        "endLine": 117,
        "endChar": 34
      },
      "revId": "9676181ec7208717edca9986e02286e752a88589",
